import{_ as t,o as s,c as a,a0 as o}from"./chunks/framework.D4fUSYzX.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"ADR 0163: A kept terminal's status keeps moving in the plane","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/0163-a-kept-terminals-status-keeps-moving-in-the-plane.md","filePath":"adr/0163-a-kept-terminals-status-keeps-moving-in-the-plane.md"}`),n={name:"adr/0163-a-kept-terminals-status-keeps-moving-in-the-plane.md"};function r(i,e,d,h,l,c){return s(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="adr-0163-a-kept-terminal-s-status-keeps-moving-in-the-plane" tabindex="-1">ADR 0163: A kept terminal&#39;s status keeps moving in the plane <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0163-a-kept-terminal-s-status-keeps-moving-in-the-plane" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR 0163: A kept terminal&#39;s status keeps moving in the plane&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Status: accepted Date: 2026-11-16 Amends ADR 0141&#39;s loss read for the kept terminal: a kept terminal whose program is lost reads Missing beside the shell or the wait the host stands in it. Amends ADR 0142&#39;s list bound: an awaiting ticket&#39;s terminal stays in the bound, so a recovered Agent is the revival the cycle sees.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The plane&#39;s herdr-core start runs without keep (ADR 0141): a lost program ends the terminal as a finished record, and the Missing flow stands for it. Nothing the plane writes turns keep on, but a terminal is host state after the start: the operator, or the host&#39;s own recovery, can keep it under the plane.</p><p>The measurement of 2026-11-16 on this machine found both gaps. A Ticket handoff the plane had started stood in a kept terminal (<code>keep: true</code> in the host&#39;s record), and the Consultation beside it stood in a second kept terminal. The Ticket&#39;s turn had settled held - cause aborted, no decision - and its settled facts, the turn log, the last message, and the completion trace, stood frozen at the settle time. The Agent recovered beside them: it went back to work and ended a second turn, and the control plane still showed the Ticket <code>held</code> on its first turn&#39;s facts. No later cycle could move it, because no later cycle read the terminal. The status of the held session never updated in the control plane.</p><p>The first gap stands in the list&#39;s bound. The merged list&#39;s per-Agent read runs over the terminal names of the in-flight Tickets and the active Consultations (ADR 0142). A Ticket whose turn settles moves to <code>awaiting</code> and leaves the bound, so the cycle reads no record of the terminal its Agent stands under. The cycle already owns the revival: an <code>awaiting</code> Ticket whose Agent reports working reopens its turn to <code>running</code>, and the turn&#39;s next settle refreshes the same completion trace. The bound, not the revival, was the gap.</p><p>The second gap stands in the record read. A kept terminal whose program is lost carries the host&#39;s loss reason - <code>signaled</code>, <code>holder_lost</code>, <code>stopped_by_restart</code>, <code>server_stop</code>, or <code>host_shutdown</code> - beside either no process id, the wait for the replacement shell the host will spawn, or the shell itself, which reports no status. The reader mapped every live record to a present Agent, so the loss read as present and <code>unknown</code>, the Missing flow never ran, and the status never moved. On the plane&#39;s own <code>--no-keep</code> start a lost program is a finished record, so the gap shows only on a terminal someone kept.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>The list&#39;s bound keeps an awaiting Ticket&#39;s terminal.</strong> The ticket states the merged list reads are the seat states and <code>awaiting</code>: <code>TICKET_LIST_STATES</code> beside <code>TICKET_SEAT_STATES</code> in the parallel module. The Consultation side of the bound stands unchanged, with <code>awaiting-response</code> and <code>closing</code> already in it. The bound costs one record read per terminal it keeps, and it stays bounded by the plane&#39;s own records.</p><p><strong>The reader reads a kept terminal whose program is lost as a dropped row - the Agent is Missing - when the live record carries a loss reason and either no process id or a program that has reported no status.</strong> A program the operator restarts in the terminal reports a status and stands present on it: the session&#39;s recovery, and the plane re-attaches to the record it reads. A host that writes no process id and no reported fact for a live record settles no loss, and the terminal reads as present.</p><p>The loss reasons are the host&#39;s kept-terminal loss vocabulary: <code>signaled</code> (a program that died to a signal without an exit code), <code>holder_lost</code>, <code>stopped_by_restart</code>, <code>server_stop</code>, and <code>host_shutdown</code>. A terminal that exits with a code is a finished record the read already maps to a settled turn, and it stays out of the loss set. A <code>spawn_pending</code> terminal is the start&#39;s wait, and it stays present.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>A held turn whose Agent recovers moves on the next cycle: the Ticket reopens to <code>running</code>, the Agent&#39;s next settle refreshes the same completion trace, and the plane shows the new last message, not the settle&#39;s frozen capture.</li><li>A kept terminal whose program dies reads Missing like a lost Agent on any host: auto mode restarts it once per episode, and manual mode stands the Missing marker and the operator&#39;s recovery.</li><li>The plane&#39;s <code>--no-keep</code> start stands unchanged (ADR 0141). This decision is what the plane owes a terminal that someone kept: keep is host state, and the plane reads the held session instead of hiding it.</li><li>A Consultation in <code>missing</code> is not re-observed: its observe list stands unchanged, a missing Consultation still takes the operator&#39;s explicit recovery, and that gap stands beside this decision, not inside it.</li><li>The suite stands both rules beside the Stub herdr world: the reader&#39;s mapping of the loss record and of the recovery report, the cycle&#39;s revival of the awaiting turn, and the auto-mode restart of a lost kept terminal (<code>test/observation.test.ts</code>). The operator&#39;s own report of 2026-11-16 is the real-host evidence for the bound gap, and the kept-terminal walk on the live host stands as the open item in the verification record.</li></ul>',13)])])}const u=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
